/**
 * Each provider's own mark, as vendored path data.
 *
 * Three words, kept apart because the module turns on the distinction. A
 * *mark* is the glyph alone, which is what fits a 16px box. A *wordmark* is the
 * company's name drawn as art, which does not: it is why Amazon is excluded
 * below, its only asset in the source set being the lowercase "aws" wordmark. A
 * *lettermark* is the fallback this file does not hold, a single initial in a
 * bordered tile, drawn by the component when no mark resolves.
 *
 * The companion to {@link providerDisplayName}: that answers what a provider is
 * called, this answers what it looks like. Same display-layer rule, so nothing
 * here changes an id, and every surface that needs the id keeps showing it.
 *
 * The geometry is vendored rather than pulled from a package. `@lobehub/icons`
 * is the source for most of it and is MIT licensed (Copyright (c) 2023
 * LobeHub), but depending on it would drag in `antd-style` and peer-require
 * `antd` and `@lobehub/ui`, a second design system this dashboard has no use
 * for. Two marks come from Simple Icons through `react-icons`, which is already
 * a dependency, because LobeHub ships no Databricks or OVH mark. One comes from
 * the vendor's own repository. `source` records which, per mark.
 *
 * Marks are monochrome and inherit the page's text ink, never a per-vendor
 * brand color: of the brand colors the sources carry, five of eleven measured
 * fall under 3:1 against one of the two theme grounds, and two are pure white.
 * LM Studio's second tone is flattened for the same reason (0.3 alpha measures
 * 2.67:1 on the dark ground and 2.00:1 on the light one); the Azure family
 * keeps its tones, which clear the bar at 5.36:1 and 3.55:1.
 *
 * A provider with no entry is not an error. Some ids have no mark anyone would
 * recognize, and an operator names their own instances, so the absence is the
 * ordinary case and the caller draws a lettermark instead.
 */
/** One filled shape of a mark. `fillOpacity` only where the source is multi-tone. */
export interface ProviderMarkShape {
  d: string
  fillOpacity?: number
}

/** A mark's geometry, in its own coordinate system. */
export interface ProviderMarkGlyph {
  /** The source's own viewBox, kept rather than refitted, so the art is untouched. */
  viewBox: string
  /** A wrapping transform the source needed. Absent for everything on a 24 grid. */
  transform?: string
  shapes: readonly ProviderMarkShape[]
  /** Where the geometry came from, for the attribution above. */
  source: string
}

/**
 * `bedrock` and `sagemaker` are deliberately absent, so they tile.
 *
 * Both are AWS credentials and the rule would give them the AWS mark, but the
 * only AWS mark in the source set is the lowercase wordmark, which is not
 * legible at 16px and less so at 14px. A lettermark "A" says as much and stays
 * readable. `maker:amazon` is left out of {@link MAKER_MARKS} for the same
 * reason, so the provider rows and the maker row agree.
 */
/**
 * Every mark's geometry, declared once.
 *
 * Shared rather than copied, because a company reached by two keys is one
 * drawing: the Azure art serves three provider ids and the Anthropic art serves
 * a provider and a maker. Copying it made the tables below 15 kB larger and let
 * an edit to one copy ship a company drawn two ways.
 */

